  @contract  arms on a note col's first pitch stop; pins (row, chan) until shift release  @ 1331
  @contract  returns true iff consumed; false lets the drain fall through (to value-digit entry)  @ 1332
  @contract  re-striking a gesture pitch toggles it off; freed slots are reused lowest-first  @ 1333
  @contract  spreadChan strikes walk channels up from home; plain strikes stack home-channel lanes  @ 1334
  @invariant  pins (col,row,part); overwrites a place keep-below, steps the sub-caret right  @ 1454
  @invariant  field re-read via cells[row] each keystroke; undo snapshots drive backspace-restore  @ 1455
  @contract  target, facility and key are remembered at take tier; the rest is per invocation  @ 2354
  @contract  with no target the whole of it is the notation snap  @ 2355
  @contract  the facility reads the target as points of the pitch line or as moves between strands  @ 2356
  @contract  purity is the moves facility's alone: how nearly a spelled interval sounds pure  @ 2357
  @contract  ambient is the moves facility's alone: the share of its sonority a strand rests on  @ 2358
  @contract  returns the steps whose empty shortlists refused the solve, else nil  @ 2359
  @contract  widen stretches those windows to the nearest points instead, so none refuses  @ 2360
  @contract  selection must be exactly one grid column; multi-col selection is a no-op  @ 3158
  @invariant  a 1-col block stays contiguous when it lands on the destination col  @ 3159
  @contract  cursor follows to the destination column (single event and selection alike)  @ 3160
  @contract  refuse if dest col has any onset in source's row extent (note: note-on; else any event)  @ 3161
  @invariant  source's row extent = selection's [r1,r2] for a block, moved event's onset row for a single  @ 3162
  @invariant  tails (either direction) clipped by tm's tail pass; never block  @ 3163
